An injector input whose source-param name ("server") equals another set's name
exercises the input namer (the local allocator). Use consumes an unprovided *Cfg,
so build's injector takes an input named after Use's parameter ("server"); the
"server" set emits a func named "server". On regeneration the re-scanned output
file must not reserve "server", so re-running plumb over its own output reproduces
it byte-for-byte.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Cfg struct{}
type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func Use(server *Cfg) *Thing { return &Thing{} }

//plumb:server
func NewServer() *int { return nil }
